---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="API Documentation — EmailFlare"
  description="Complete EmailFlare API reference: authentication, POST /v1/send, templates, themes, error codes, and troubleshooting — from zero to first email in minutes."
  keywords="emailflare api docs, email api documentation, post v1 send, emailflare authentication, api key types, email template api"
  canonical="https://emailflare.dev/docs"
  ogUrl="https://emailflare.dev/docs"
  ogType="article"
  navType="docs"
>

<style is:global>
  /* ── DOCS PAGE ────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* ── HERO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .docs-hero {
    background: oklch(14% 0.016 48);
    padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) 0 clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .docs-badge {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px;
    background: oklch(22% 0.04 48 / 0.8);
    color: oklch(68% 0.14 55);
    font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500;
    padding: 4px 13px;
    border-radius: 100px;
    border: 1px solid oklch(35% 0.08 55 / 0.5);
    margin-bottom: 22px;
  }

  .docs-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: oklch(95% 0.008 58);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .docs-hero h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--orange); }

  .docs-hero-sub {
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: oklch(58% 0.01 58);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  .docs-hero-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* ── DOCS LAYOUT ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .docs-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 230px 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 24px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .docs-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .docs-sidebar { display: none; }
  }

  .docs-sidebar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 82px;
    padding: 32px 0 32px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
    margin-right: 0;
  }

  .sidebar-label {
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding: 0 16px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .sidebar-nav { list-style: none; }
  .sidebar-nav li a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 16px;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-left: 2px solid transparent;
    transition: color 0.12s, border-color 0.12s;
  }
  .sidebar-nav li a:hover { color: var(--text); border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .sidebar-nav li a.active { color: var(--text); border-left-color: var(--orange); font-weight: 500; }

  /* ── MAIN CONTENT ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .docs-main { padding: 32px 0 56px 40px; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) { .docs-main { padding: 32px 0 48px; } }

  /* ── DOC SECTION ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .doc-section {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .doc-section-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 18px 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-alt);
  }

  .doc-section-header h2 {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    flex: 1;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .anchor-link {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }
  .anchor-link:hover { color: var(--orange); }

  .doc-body { padding: 24px; }
  .doc-body > p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .doc-body > *:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .doc-body > *:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .doc-body p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .doc-body h3 {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    margin: 22px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .doc-body h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .doc-body ul {
    padding-left: 18px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .doc-body ul li {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }

  .doc-body ul li::marker { color: var(--orange); }

  .doc-body code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    background: oklch(93% 0.006 60);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--orange-dark);
  }

  /* TABLE ── */
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 14px 0; }

  .doc-body table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; }
  .doc-body th {
    text-align: left; padding: 9px 12px;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-alt);
  }
  .doc-body td { padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--text); vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.6; }
  .doc-body tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .doc-body td:first-child code { background: var(--orange-light); border-color: var(--orange-mid); color: var(--orange-dark); }

  /* PILLS ── */
  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 100px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .pill-req  { background: oklch(93% 0.04 24); color: oklch(42% 0.14 24); border: 1px solid oklch(78% 0.1 24 / 0.5); }
  .pill-opt  { background: oklch(93% 0.004 58); color: var(--text-muted); border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .pill-cond { background: oklch(94% 0.04 80); color: oklch(38% 0.12 70); border: 1px solid oklch(78% 0.1 80 / 0.5); }

  /* CALLOUT ── */
  .callout {
    display: flex; gap: 11px; align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 13px 16px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 16px 0;
  }
  .callout-icon { font-size: 15px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .callout-orange { background: var(--orange-light); border: 1px solid var(--orange-mid); color: var(--orange-dark); }
  .callout-green  { background: oklch(95% 0.012 150); border: 1px solid oklch(82% 0.08 150); color: oklch(36% 0.1 150); }
  .callout-blue   { background: oklch(94% 0.02 230); border: 1px solid oklch(80% 0.08 230); color: oklch(42% 0.14 230); }

  /* CODE BLOCK ── */
  .code-block {
    background: oklch(14% 0.016 48);
    border: 1px solid oklch(24% 0.016 48);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.85;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 14px 0;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }

  .cb-cmd    { color: oklch(82% 0.06 58); }
  .cb-str    { color: oklch(74% 0.12 140); }
  .cb-key    { color: oklch(78% 0.12 230); }
  .cb-punct  { color: oklch(62% 0.06 58); }
  .cb-num    { color: oklch(74% 0.12 82); }
  .cb-header { color: oklch(72% 0.1 58); }
  .cb-plain  { color: oklch(75% 0.01 58); }

  /* STATUS ── */
  .status-err  { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: oklch(50% 0.14 24); background: oklch(94% 0.04 24); border: 1px solid oklch(80% 0.1 24 / 0.5); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; }
  .status-warn { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; color: oklch(48% 0.12 70); background: oklch(94% 0.04 80); border: 1px solid oklch(80% 0.1 80 / 0.5); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; }

  /* KEY TYPES ── */
  .key-types { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; margin: 14px 0; }
  @media (max-width: 500px) { .key-types { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .key-type-card {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 14px 16px;
  }

  .key-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
    padding: 2px 9px; border-radius: 100px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .key-badge-test { background: oklch(93% 0.04 80); color: oklch(40% 0.12 70); border: 1px solid oklch(78% 0.1 80 / 0.5); }
  .key-badge-live { background: oklch(93% 0.04 150); color: oklch(36% 0.1 150); border: 1px solid oklch(78% 0.08 150 / 0.5); }

  .key-type-card p { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }

  /* QUICKSTART STEPS ── */
  .qs-steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; margin: 14px 0; }
  .qs-step { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: start; }
  .qs-num {
    width: 26px; height: 26px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--orange-light);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--orange-mid);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--orange-dark);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .qs-body { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; padding-top: 3px; }

  /* GUIDE CARDS ── */
  .guide-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin: 14px 0; }
  .guide-card {
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 14px 16px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text);
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .guide-card:hover { border-color: var(--orange-mid); }
  .guide-card .gc-label { font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--orange); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .guide-card h4 { font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .guide-card p  { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }

  /* THEME LIST ── */
  .theme-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 12px 0; }
  .theme-chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px;
    background: var(--bg-alt);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 100px;
    padding: 5px 14px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .theme-dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; flex-shrink: 0; }
</style>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="docs-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="docs-badge">Documentation v1</div>
      <h1>From zero to <em>first delivered email</em> in minutes.</h1>
      <p class="docs-hero-sub">
        Complete API reference — authentication, <code style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12px;background:oklch(24% 0.03 48);border:1px solid oklch(32% 0.02 48);color:oklch(74% 0.1 55);padding:1px 5px;border-radius:4px;">/v1/send</code>, templates, themes,
        error codes, and troubleshooting. Everything you need to integrate with EmailFlare.
      </p>
      <div class="docs-hero-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#quickstart">Get started →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/0xdps/emailflare" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- DOCS LAYOUT -->
  <div style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <!-- SIDEBAR -->
      <aside class="docs-sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-label">On this page</div>
        <ul class="sidebar-nav">
          <li><a href="#quickstart">Quickstart</a></li>
          <li><a href="#authentication">Authentication</a></li>
          <li><a href="#api-send">POST /v1/send</a></li>
          <li><a href="#templates">Templates &amp; themes</a></li>
          <li><a href="#errors">Error responses</a></li>
          <li><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></li>
        </ul>
      </aside>

      <!-- MAIN -->
      <main class="docs-main">

        <!-- 1. QUICKSTART -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="quickstart">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>Quickstart</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#quickstart">#quickstart</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <p>Get to a working send in four steps — from a fresh deploy to a delivered email.</p>
            <div class="qs-steps">
              <div class="qs-step">
                <div class="qs-num">1</div>
                <div class="qs-body"><strong>Deploy EmailFlare</strong> — on Cloudflare Workers (primary) or Docker Compose (secondary). See the <a href="/cloudflare" style="color:var(--orange);text-decoration:none;">Cloudflare Workers guide</a> or the <a href="https://github.com/0xdps/emailflare/blob/trunk/docs/SELF_HOSTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:var(--orange);text-decoration:none;">self-hosting docs</a>.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="qs-step">
                <div class="qs-num">2</div>
                <div class="qs-body"><strong>Add a sending domain</strong> — go to the Domains page in the admin UI, enter your domain, and complete the DNS verification steps Cloudflare provides.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="qs-step">
                <div class="qs-num">3</div>
                <div class="qs-body"><strong>Create an API key</strong> — go to the Keys page in the admin UI, click <em>New key</em>, and choose a scope. Copy the key — it won't be shown again.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="qs-step">
                <div class="qs-num">4</div>
                <div class="qs-body"><strong>Send your first email</strong> — <code>POST /v1/send</code> with your key in the <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> header. Start with a test key and <code>eftest_</code> prefix to skip Cloudflare credentials.</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="guide-cards">
              <a class="guide-card" href="/cloudflare">
                <div class="gc-label">Deploy</div>
                <h4>Cloudflare Workers setup</h4>
                <p>One-command deploy to the edge with D1, KV, and the admin UI.</p>
              </a>
              <a class="guide-card" href="/cloudflare-token">
                <div class="gc-label">Required</div>
                <h4>Cloudflare API token guide</h4>
                <p>Exact permissions needed for Email Sending, DNS, and routing rules.</p>
              </a>
              <a class="guide-card" href="https://github.com/0xdps/emailflare/blob/trunk/docs/SELF_HOSTING.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                <div class="gc-label">Secondary</div>
                <h4>Docker self-hosting guide</h4>
                <p>Full Compose stack — container, volumes, environment variables.</p>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. AUTHENTICATION -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="authentication">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>Authentication</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#authentication">#authentication</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <p>All <code>/v1/send</code> requests must include a bearer token in the <code>Authorization</code> header.</p>

            <div class="code-block"><span class="cb-header">Authorization</span><span class="cb-plain">: Bearer </span><span class="cb-str">eflive_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</span></div>

            <h3>Key types</h3>
            <div class="key-types">
              <div class="key-type-card">
                <div class="key-badge key-badge-test">⚗ test key</div>
                <p>Prefix: <code>eftest_</code>. Sends are stored in the admin dashboard — no Cloudflare credentials required. Browse, preview HTML, and manage test emails from the built-in Test Mailbox page.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="key-type-card">
                <div class="key-badge key-badge-live">✓ live key</div>
                <p>Prefix: <code>eflive_</code>. Sends go through Cloudflare Email Sending. Requires valid <code>CF_API_TOKEN</code> and verified domain.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="callout callout-orange">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              Domain-scoped keys can only send from domains listed in that key's permissions. Requests with an unauthorized domain return <code>403</code>.
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 3. SEND API -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="api-send">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>POST /v1/send</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#api-send">#api-send</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <p>The single endpoint for all transactional sends. Use <code>templateSlug</code> / <code>templateId</code> for stored templates, or pass raw <code>html</code> / <code>text</code> directly.</p>

            <h3>Request fields</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Field</th>
                    <th>Type</th>
                    <th>Required</th>
                    <th>Description</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>from</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-req">required</span></td>
                    <td>Sender email address. Must match a verified domain authorized for your key.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>fromName</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Display name shown in the From header, e.g. <code>Acme Inc.</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>to</code></td>
                    <td>string or string[]</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-req">required</span></td>
                    <td>Recipient address or array of up to 50 addresses. Duplicates are deduplicated.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>subject</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Overrides the template subject. Required for raw <code>html</code>/<code>text</code> sends.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>templateSlug</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-cond">conditional</span></td>
                    <td>Stable slug-based template reference. Preferred for application code.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>templateId</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-cond">conditional</span></td>
                    <td>Internal ID-based template reference. Use <code>templateSlug</code> when possible.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>themeId</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Applies a built-in colour theme to layout-based templates. See <a href="#templates" style="color:var(--orange);">theme list</a> below. Defaults to <code>default</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>variables</code></td>
                    <td>object</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Key/value map for <code>&#123;&#123;variable&#125;&#125;</code> interpolation in subject and body.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>html</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-cond">conditional</span></td>
                    <td>Raw HTML body. Used when not referencing a template.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>text</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-cond">conditional</span></td>
                    <td>Plain-text body. Can be combined with <code>html</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>replyTo</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Reply-to address for the recipient.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>listId</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Audience list ID. Attaches a one-click <code>List-Unsubscribe</code> header with a per-recipient token, so the recipient can unsubscribe (globally suppressed for all future sends).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>listUnsubscribe</code></td>
                    <td>string</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Override the unsubscribe URL (e.g. your own <code>https://…/unsubscribe</code>). Passed through verbatim.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code>listUnsubscribePost</code></td>
                    <td>boolean</td>
                    <td><span class="pill pill-opt">optional</span></td>
                    <td>Adds <code>List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click</code> (RFC 8058). Defaults to <code>true</code> when <code>listId</code> is set.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="callout callout-orange">
              <span class="callout-icon">⚡</span>
              At least one of <code>templateSlug</code>, <code>templateId</code>, <code>html</code>, or <code>text</code> must be provided.
            </div>

            <h3>cURL</h3>
            <div class="code-block"><span class="cb-cmd">curl -X POST https://your-emailflare.com/v1/send</span> \
  -H <span class="cb-str">"Authorization: Bearer eflive_xxx"</span> \
  -H <span class="cb-str">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
  -d <span class="cb-str">'</span><span class="cb-punct">{</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"from"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>         <span class="cb-str">"hello@yourdomain.com"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"fromName"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>     <span class="cb-str">"Acme"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"to"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>           <span class="cb-str">"alex@example.com"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"templateSlug"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">"welcome"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"themeId"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>      <span class="cb-str">"ocean"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"variables"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>    <span class="cb-punct">&#123;</span> <span class="cb-key">"name"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">"Alex"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span> <span class="cb-key">"appName"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">"Acme"</span> <span class="cb-punct">&#125;</span>
  <span class="cb-str">'&#125;</span></div>

            <h3>fetch (JavaScript)</h3>
            <div class="code-block"><span class="cb-plain">const res = await fetch(</span><span class="cb-str">'https://your-emailflare.com/v1/send'</span><span class="cb-plain">, &#123;</span>
  <span class="cb-key">method</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">'POST'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
  <span class="cb-key">headers</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-punct">&#123;</span>
    <span class="cb-str">'Authorization'</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">'Bearer eflive_xxx'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-str">'Content-Type'</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>  <span class="cb-str">'application/json'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
  <span class="cb-punct">&#125;,</span>
  <span class="cb-key">body</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-plain">JSON.stringify(&#123;</span>
    <span class="cb-key">from</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>         <span class="cb-str">'hello@yourdomain.com'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">to</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>           <span class="cb-str">'alex@example.com'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">templateSlug</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">'welcome'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">themeId</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>      <span class="cb-str">'ocean'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">variables</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>    <span class="cb-punct">&#123;</span> <span class="cb-key">name</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">'Alex'</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span> <span class="cb-key">appName</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">'Acme'</span> <span class="cb-punct">&#125;,</span>
  <span class="cb-plain">&#125;),</span>
<span class="cb-plain">&#125;);</span>
<span class="cb-plain">const data = await res.json();</span></div>

            <h3>Response (200)</h3>
            <div class="code-block"><span class="cb-punct">&#123;</span>
  <span class="cb-key">"results"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-punct">[&#123;</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"to"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span>   <span class="cb-str">"alex@example.com"</span><span class="cb-punct">,</span>
    <span class="cb-key">"cfId"</span><span class="cb-punct">:</span> <span class="cb-str">"cf_msg_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"</span>
  <span class="cb-punct">&#125;]</span>
<span class="cb-punct">&#125;</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. TEMPLATES & THEMES -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="templates">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>Templates &amp; themes</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#templates">#templates</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <p>EmailFlare ships 50 layout-based templates built with React Email. Reference them by their <code>templateSlug</code>. Pass <code>themeId</code> to switch colour palettes per send — no CSS edits needed.</p>

            <h3>Available themes</h3>
            <div class="theme-list">
              <div class="theme-chip"><span class="theme-dot" style="background:#f97316;"></span><code>default</code></div>
              <div class="theme-chip"><span class="theme-dot" style="background:#0ea5e9;"></span><code>ocean</code></div>
              <div class="theme-chip"><span class="theme-dot" style="background:#16a34a;"></span><code>forest</code></div>
              <div class="theme-chip"><span class="theme-dot" style="background:#7c3aed;"></span><code>violet</code></div>
              <div class="theme-chip"><span class="theme-dot" style="background:#334155;"></span><code>slate</code></div>
            </div>

            <div class="callout callout-green">
              <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
              Use the admin Playground to preview any template with any theme before sending to real recipients.
            </div>

            <h3>Template reference tips</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Prefer <code>templateSlug</code> over <code>templateId</code> — slugs are stable across restores.</li>
              <li>Variable names follow the <code>&#123;&#123;camelCase&#125;&#125;</code> convention used in the template body and subject.</li>
              <li>If a variable is missing from the payload, it renders as the literal <code>&#123;&#123;variableName&#125;&#125;</code> placeholder.</li>
              <li><code>themeId</code> only applies to layout-based templates. Custom HTML templates ignore it.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 5. ERRORS -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="errors">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>Error responses</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#errors">#errors</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <div class="table-wrap">
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th>Status</th>
                    <th>Meaning</th>
                    <th>Common cause</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-err">401</span></td>
                    <td>Unauthorized</td>
                    <td>Missing or invalid <code>Authorization</code> header.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-err">403</span></td>
                    <td>Forbidden</td>
                    <td>Key scope does not authorize the sender domain.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-warn">404</span></td>
                    <td>Not found</td>
                    <td><code>templateSlug</code> or <code>templateId</code> does not exist.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-warn">422</span></td>
                    <td>Validation error</td>
                    <td>Missing required fields or invalid email format.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-warn">429</span></td>
                    <td>Rate limited</td>
                    <td>Per-key send limit reached. Check <code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code> header.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-err">502</span></td>
                    <td>All recipients failed</td>
                    <td>Downstream delivery failed for every address in the request.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><span class="status-err">500</span></td>
                    <td>Server error</td>
                    <td>Unexpected backend error — check container logs.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <p style="margin-top:12px;">Rate limiting headers returned on every <code>/v1/send</code> response:</p>
            <div class="code-block"><span class="cb-header">X-RateLimit-Limit</span><span class="cb-plain">:     </span><span class="cb-num">100</span>
<span class="cb-header">X-RateLimit-Remaining</span><span class="cb-plain">: </span><span class="cb-num">97</span>
<span class="cb-header">X-RateLimit-Reset</span><span class="cb-plain">:     </span><span class="cb-num">1746403200</span></div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 6. TROUBLESHOOTING -->
        <section class="doc-section" id="troubleshooting">
          <div class="doc-section-header">
            <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
            <a class="anchor-link" href="#troubleshooting">#troubleshooting</a>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-body">
            <h3>401 on /v1/send</h3>
            <p>Confirm the header is exactly <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code> with no extra spaces. Verify the key is marked active on the Keys page.</p>

            <h3>403 with a domain-scoped key</h3>
            <p>The <code>from</code> address domain must be included in the key's allowed domains. Create a <code>global</code> scoped key to bypass domain restrictions while debugging.</p>

            <h3>Template not found (404)</h3>
            <p>Copy the slug exactly from the Templates page — it is case-sensitive. System templates use slugs like <code>welcome</code>, <code>magic-link</code>, <code>otp</code>.</p>

            <h3>Theme not applied to email</h3>
            <p><code>themeId</code> only works with layout-based (built-in) templates. For custom HTML templates the field is ignored — you control the styles directly in the HTML body.</p>

            <h3>Sends succeed in test mode but fail in live mode</h3>
            <p>Test keys (<code>eftest_</code>) store emails in the dashboard and don't require Cloudflare credentials. Live keys use Cloudflare Email Sending — ensure <code>CF_API_TOKEN</code> has the correct permissions and the sender domain is verified. See the <a href="/cloudflare-token" style="color:var(--orange);text-decoration:none;">Cloudflare token guide →</a></p>
            <p style="margin-top:8px;">Test emails are stored in the built-in Test Mailbox page in the admin UI — no external service needed.</p>

            <h3>Database errors in logs</h3>
            <p>If you see <em>"This SQL statement is not allowed on /query endpoint"</em>, upgrade to the latest EmailFlare image — this was a bug fixed in the backend send route.</p>

            <div class="callout callout-orange">
              <span class="callout-icon">📋</span>
              Always check container logs first: <code>docker compose logs -f emailflare</code>. Most issues are visible in the startup or request output.
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

      </main>
    </div>
  </div>

